WEBVTT

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.310
Pardon me, sir.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.540
There was a call from Yoshida-sama 
from the committee earlier this morning.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.270
How many times must I tell him 
to go through my assistant?

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.380
Is something the matter, sir?

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.870
<b>To Matsuda Kazuo-sama</b>

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:21.870
<b>I know your secrets. 
If you don't want the world to know them, 
please transfer ten million yen as soon as possible.</b>

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.870
"I know your secrets."

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.420
"If you don't want the world to know them, 
please transfer ten million yen."

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:27.630
What the hell is this?

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.610
Is it one of those "virus" things?

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:32.790
Rather elaborate for blackmail.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.260
Sir, would you let me handle this?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:40.970
I know someone who's familiar
with this sort of nonsense.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:16.260
<b>#07  Leadoff Hitter</b>

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.490
Oh, right. So the cyberterrorist 
cell you wanted me to look into...

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:18.530
Right. M3.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.240
Well, the job was a real pain in the neck.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:25.270
Experts tend to have 
tougher security, y'know?

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:27.090
But you were able to get in, right?

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.080
Naturally.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:33.190
This is top secret data that 
one of their associates had.

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:35.300
It should come in handy.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:39.300
For an officer who's investigating 
cybercrime, anyway.

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.720
It just might.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.680
Well, let's trade this for that 
hacking incident last week.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:51.650
It seems like some kind 
of list, but it's encrypted.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.090
That sort of thing is more 
up your alley, right?

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:56.710
We'll see if we can decipher it.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.650
Maru-san?

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:03.050
What? Saito-kun's been arrested?

00:03:03.050 --> 00:03:05.340
<i>Seems it was real bad stuff.</i>

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.690
<i>He was threatening politicians 
over the internet,</i>

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.620
<i>distributing private nude pics and so on...</i>

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.940
<i>So some sort of cybercrime 
something-or-other came for him.</i>

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.180
The Counter Cybercrime Unit?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.550
<b>Saeki Cosmetic Surgery Clinic</b>

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.550
<b>Consultations 
concluded for today</b>

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:21.550
Didn't expect to get a call from you, Doc.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.510
Sorry to drag you all the way out here.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.940
But I'd like you to look into something.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.740
Who are they?

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:31.940
They all seem to be homeless.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:35.020
The bodies were delivered by courier.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.580
Along with a message that I had to 
dispose of them or be killed myself.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.950
Well, that's creepy as hell.

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:45.030
I do clean up bodies, but this...

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.450
And you have no idea who it might've been?

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:48.370
No.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.660
But I think it's the same 
person sending the bodies.

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:53.000
They used the exact same method.

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:59.670
Identifying anyone this badly beaten
is gonna be a real pain in the ass...

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.340
I have a job for you.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.680
Who's the target?

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.940
A hacker named Macro Hard.

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:17.530
He's sniffing around politicians 
that we've been backing.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:20.180
I'll have Siva look into it right away.

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:23.290
You're still working with that psychopath?

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.410
The organization recognizes his skill 
with cracking computer security.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.770
But he has personality issues.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:33.570
And that washed-up boxer of yours...

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:35.500
No telling when he's going 
to screw something up.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.980
I could tell him to see a psychiatrist...

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.210
As long as I can send the 
bill to your organization.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:44.980
Well, just don't screw up.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:51.680
<b>Nishijin Chuo Shopping District</b>

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:53.930
<b>PC Doctor's Factory</b>

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:57.900
Hey, Chegaru-san!

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.400
<b>We are closed for today. 
Thank you for understanding.</b>

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.010
What are you watching, Irasawa?

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.340
The match from the other day.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:25.090
That's all you're watching? You're 
the one who told me to record it.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:28.550
I didn't tell you to stare at it 24 hours a day.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.490
"If you get the urge to kill, watch 
the video and let that tide you over."

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:35.730
So much for that idea.

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.690
Who's this?

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:41.690
Just some NEET.

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:44.850
I put a little spice into his life.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.950
Well, that's enough fun and 
games. It's time to work.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.790
Who is it this time?

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:52.440
Macro Hard.

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:53.910
What a stupid name.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.410
He apparently has information 
on our organization.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.380
Find him, and then...

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.770
The usual routine.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.830
Ta-da! Your costume for the play is ready!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.470
Oh, my! You look so cute!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.820
What's wrong?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.940
The play got canceled.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.930
Oh, no. Why?

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.430
Giria-chan's mom made a fuss,

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.780
saying, "Why isn't my daughter the heroine?"

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:29.860
Oh, dear...

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:34.620
Then they changed the script so
all the girls could be heroines.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:40.160
They were going to make the prince a playboy 
and have all the princesses fight over him.

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:42.000
Ew, how vulgar.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.260
The principal called it off in the end,

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:47.250
so we're all singing instead.

00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.180
So... I'm sorry.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:55.850
It's okay, Misaki. Don't let it bother you.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.980
But what am I going to do with this?

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:04.550
I'm telling you, I wasn't arrested! 
I went in for questioning voluntarily!

00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:07.660
But the cops did show up, right?

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.280
So what kind of cybercrime were you into?

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.810
My computer was used to send out 
death threats, bomb threats,

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:17.780
and other stuff over internet message boards.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:20.120
And when they looked into it...

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:24.660
It was loaded with pics of naked little girls!

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.400
You're a real freak now!

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.140
I'm telling you, it wasn't me!

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:31.470
There were a bunch of folders 
on it that I had no idea about!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:36.430
So he almost got nailed for a 
crime he had nothing to do with?

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.550
It was done with a remote-access virus.

00:07:39.550 --> 00:07:43.020
A hacker probably sent it in an email.

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:45.780
The internet's a scary place.

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:51.100
Saito was grateful, though. 
You talked to the cops for him?

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.580
I have an acquaintance 
who was involved, so...

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:55.280
It was still nice of you to do it.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:57.660
I even have a reward for you!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:58.740
For me?

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.250
What the hell is this?

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:04.350
He thought you could use a spare.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.640
Except that my hair is natural.

00:08:07.640 --> 00:08:11.260
Jiro put it together for Misaki's play.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:13.610
Seems it got canceled, though.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:16.550
Kind of a cute family story, ain't it?

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:19.000
Family, huh?

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.980
What? You still haven't made up with yours?

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:24.270
I wouldn't know where to begin.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.980
You ought to know that, Maru-san.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:34.400
<b>Banba Private Investigations</b>

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:34.400
So, what can I help you with?

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:37.410
I want you to find this man.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:41.370
He's the son of the family I serve.

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.580
For certain reasons, he had to 
go into hiding eight years ago.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.950
Hey, isn't that...

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.800
Yeah. I see the resemblance.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.760
The hair... the eyes...

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:54.410
That means...

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.680
Oh, if you're busy...

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.260
Young master!

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.390
"Young master"?!

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:09.770
Pardon me.

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.780
Whoa! What are you trying to do?!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.260
We're on the third floor!

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:23.830
It's good to see you again, young master.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.260
Yagi...

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:30.900
I guess you <i>are</i> a former hitman.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.560
All I've ever been is a servant.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:35.170
Back then, as well as now.

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:37.630
Who the hell are you?

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:42.510
Well, well, I had no idea you were 
friends of the young master.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:46.480
Thank you for looking out for him.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:52.320
I don't get what's going on, but I'm glad 
you found who you were looking for.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:56.950
So the mushroom is the son 
of some rich family, huh?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:01.630
I forgot to give him the data...

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:04.150
That's why I called Enokida-kun over.

00:10:04.150 --> 00:10:05.000
Data?

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.850
Y'know the thing with those homeless bodies?

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:10.290
I wanted him to take a look 
using their fingerprints.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.410
It's the Doc.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:17.420
What is it?

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:20.390
Another body.

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:28.030
Looks like it's done.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:29.560
You mean the Macro Hard thing?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.510
Irasawa sent me video of the kill again.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:37.410
Someone likes to show off.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:40.380
So, did you find anything?

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.530
This is Macro Hard's data.

00:10:42.980 --> 00:10:46.280
It's mostly blackmail material.

00:10:46.280 --> 00:10:49.010
He cracked into computers and 
was demanding money in return

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:50.870
for keeping people's secrets.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:54.030
That's a lot of famous names.

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:57.670
Politicians, stars, pro athletes...

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:00.740
The problem was this one, though.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.300
Matsuda?

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:04.630
The one in the House of Representatives?

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.370
Yep.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.920
Looking at the data,

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:12.090
his only son once hacked the 
Metropolitan Police's database,

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:13.650
and got arrested for it.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:18.610
What a great kid. I assume it was covered up?

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:23.610
Yeah, but that's not the fun 
part. It's the son's MO.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.830
It looks a lot like Black Leg's.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:30.480
The one on the blacklist?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.670
Black Leg Nameko.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:36.840
I'd been trying to find the guy who was 
looking into our organization lately,

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.800
and the similarities in their 
hacking got me wondering.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.610
About Black Leg?

00:11:42.610 --> 00:11:47.410
Yep. And what I eventually found 
was this net café in Nakasu.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.980
And I found who we're looking for.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.030
I think this is him.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:11:58.980
Black Leg.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.200
What brings you all the way out here?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.410
This was found on the master's computer.

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:11.370
<b>To Matsuda Kazuo-sama

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:11.370
He's apparently been hacked.

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:14.130
And you think I did it?

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.340
Surely you jest.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:19.280
Someone with your abilities wouldn't 
need to stoop to this level.

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.130
True enough.

00:12:20.640 --> 00:12:25.980
I was hoping you could help 
me track down the culprit.

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:28.350
Why would I do anything to help him?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:31.310
<b>Keep Out</b>

00:12:29.170 --> 00:12:31.310
You still resent him?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:35.270
Of course I do. I was killed...

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.420
by my own father.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:43.130
So what's all this? Why are we here?

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.330
You're gonna kill me?

00:12:50.940 --> 00:12:53.540
It's the master's orders.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.000
Because I'm in the way?

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:08.970
Yagi?

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.100
Please flee.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:18.790
A ticket to Fukuoka. 
I have acquaintances in Hakata.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:23.530
If you find yourself in trouble, turn 
to them. I'm certain they will help you.

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:27.700
Please be well, young master.

00:13:29.890 --> 00:13:32.070
I'm not gonna believe you if you say

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:36.120
you forgot pointing that 
gun at me eight years ago.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.620
Weren't you merely reaping 
what you'd sown?

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:43.150
It was you who committed crimes and 
tried to sully your father's name.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:47.570
Put any kid in puberty through 
that kind of intense "education,"

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:49.970
and they're bound to act out.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.860
You chose poorly in how 
you acted out, though.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:57.270
Hacking the Metropolitan Police at a time 
that was critical for your father...

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.980
I did it because I knew the timing.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.150
A scandal in the middle 
of an election campaign...

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.890
Bet that was expensive to cover up.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:09.660
Anyway, this doesn't have 
anything to do with me.

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:15.950
I'll never forget what I 
overheard him say once...

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.920
"That boy is sick. And there's 
no cure for what he has."

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:23.880
Young master... No, Enokida-san...

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:28.050
I don't want you to get the wrong impression.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.760
I've come here to offer you a job.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:37.190
If it's insufficient, I can pay double.

00:14:39.090 --> 00:14:41.540
If you're a professional in this world,

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:44.150
I advise against letting personal 
matters disrupt business.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:50.060
Okay. I'll find your hacker in a flash.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:52.820
Go have fun touring 
Fukuoka in the meantime.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:57.000
<b>PC Doctor's Factory</b>

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.000
You ever hear of Flammulina?

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.710
<b>Open only for 
limited hours today.</b>

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.710
<b>We apologize for 
any inconvenience.</b>

00:14:57.590 --> 00:15:00.710
It's a data-sniffing virus 
that Black Leg came up with.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.760
It infects the machine when the mark 
downloads videos or images.

00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.570
It rings a bell.

00:15:06.570 --> 00:15:12.490
The virus that Matsuda Kazuo's son used 
was basically the first version of that.

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:14.550
And what happened to him?

00:15:14.550 --> 00:15:17.370
The records say he died eight years ago.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:21.230
But it wouldn't take much to disguise him,

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:25.480
so he ran away to Hakata
and is going by "Black Leg" now.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.110
It's actually easier to believe 
that, wouldn't you say?

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:38.870
Kuroiwa Manabu. Worked for the 
Chuo ward office in 7-chome.

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:42.410
So this one wasn't homeless, huh?

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:44.920
And his personal effects were still on him.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:45.840
His phone, too.

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:48.970
So it wasn't a mugging...

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.550
What the hell's the point, then?

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.220
We can always check it out.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.180
His address is pretty near here, anyway.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.600
It's open...

00:16:06.710 --> 00:16:08.850
Someone went nuts in here.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.990
Mushroom?

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:23.750
Kuroiwa Manabu. He was a hacker 
who went by the name Macro Hard.

00:16:24.390 --> 00:16:26.910
I was looking for him for another case.

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.000
Is that what that old guy wanted?

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.430
More or less.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:32.230
But from the look of things,

00:16:32.230 --> 00:16:35.500
his PC and anything else that could 
be used as evidence was taken.

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.130
What about his phone?

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.690
I don't know the passcode, though.

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:44.020
That won't be a problem, I assure you.

00:16:44.430 --> 00:16:45.410
There it is...

00:16:46.340 --> 00:16:49.650
I thought I felt something watching us.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.210
Looks like a hidden camera.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:02.160
I'll get it for you. Since I'm taller.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:05.120
Excuse me? I'm obviously taller.

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.580
Want to test that theory?

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.130
See? I'm taller!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.190
No, it's just your high heels!

00:17:12.190 --> 00:17:15.580
Like you can talk with those chunky soles!

00:17:15.580 --> 00:17:18.260
I don't think the difference 
is big enough to matter.

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:23.980
<i>Huh? Who the hell—</i>

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.930
Wonder who these guys are...

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.980
Can't see their faces from this angle.

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.110
They were after his PC, all right.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.890
If he had a hidden camera 
set up in his own place,

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.640
he probably knew people would be after him.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:47.050
I think someone he'd tried to blackmail 
sent professional hitmen after him.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:50.540
So they grab the PC to keep things quiet...

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.570
Not sure how this connects to 
the homeless murders, though.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:18:01.030
Sorry, guys, but this wraps up my 
case quite nicely. Although...

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.890
Macro Hard has been taken care of.

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:05.980
I see.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.380
There was one issue, though.

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:11.800
It seems Black Leg lives in this town.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:14.610
Black Leg? You're sure about that?

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:19.060
It was indicated by the intel 
that Macro Hard had.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.570
What should we do?

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:27.860
He's a threat to us, no doubt. 
Better to take care of him quickly.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.080
You took care of the body, I take it?

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.190
Yeah. Had a pro do it.

00:18:43.190 --> 00:18:44.180
All right, then.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.240
On to the next job.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:48.370
We're going to take care of Black Leg.

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.150
That's what I like to hear!

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:54.240
Don't make it obvious.

00:18:54.240 --> 00:18:56.540
If he notices us, we'll never get to him.

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:59.450
I could always screw with the signal

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:02.680
all over Fukuoka to keep him 
from counter-hacking us.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:04.700
Wouldn't that take you down, too?

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.630
Being a hacker seems like a real drag.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:11.230
With no PC, they're as puny as anyone else.

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.880
That's it.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:20.800
Irasawa has a point. If we 
keep him from using a PC...

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.430
<i>This is about the list you 
gave us the other day.</i>

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.150
You were able to decrypt it?

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:28.750
<i>Yes. I've sent you a copy.</i>

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:33.100
It's a list of hackers from all over the world.

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:35.870
M3 has a secret side to their business,

00:19:35.870 --> 00:19:38.990
which involves sending operatives 
out to locations across the globe

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:42.450
to kill any hackers who might do them harm.

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:47.260
Are we talking about a group of assassins 
that specializes in killing hackers?

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:49.410
Then, this list...

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:52.870
<i>Exactly. It's a hit list.</i>

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:57.330
I see Macro Hard's name. That confirms it.

00:19:57.330 --> 00:19:59.410
<i>Take a look at the third page.</i>

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:07.430
<i>M3 is after you, too, Enokida-san.</i>

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:13.570
Find anything?

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.220
It wouldn't kill you to—

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:16.770
Huh?!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.540
What's up?

00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:18.190
Look!

00:20:18.190 --> 00:20:23.200
<b>Shadyjob.com</b>

00:20:19.970 --> 00:20:23.200
"Five million to whoever brings in this man..."

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:24.740
What's the big deal?

00:20:25.870 --> 00:20:27.470
<b>Gender:</b> Male
 <b>Height:</b> 165-170cm, thin
<b>Characteristics:</b> Blonde hair, teenager 
<b>Known Location:</b> Nakasu 3-chome 7-24, 
Hakata Ward, Fukuoka City, 
5th floor of the Gates Building

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.710
Five million for this punk?

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:37.460
Piece of cake!

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.170
Five million?

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:42.920
Whoa!

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:48.470
Ow!

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:03.400
You all right?

00:21:03.970 --> 00:21:05.780
Glad we made it in time.

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.410
Banba-san...

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:09.910
"M3"?

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.670
Some kind of anti-hacker hitman group.

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.710
I thought someone might've been on my trail...

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:19.460
For now, I need to take down this post.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:23.350
What's wrong?

00:21:23.350 --> 00:21:24.840
It was a trap.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.340
A trap?

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:26.340
<b>Location:</b>

00:21:26.340 --> 00:21:29.020
I've been infected with a virus.

00:21:29.020 --> 00:21:32.740
As long as I'm online,
it broadcasts my location data.

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:35.220
Meaning it'll be obvious where you are?

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:39.620
Just gotta disconnect, then, right?

00:21:39.620 --> 00:21:41.770
That's what they want me to do.

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:46.180
A hacker can't do anything 
without a computer.

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:54.910
That should've been a double play!

00:21:55.740 --> 00:22:00.300
How could they screw that up? It was 
obvious that the runner was bait!

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:04.230
If they'd thrown to second, 
it would've been two outs!

00:22:04.930 --> 00:22:05.900
<i>Bait?</i>

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:09.010
Banba-san, I'm gonna get out here.

00:22:09.530 --> 00:22:10.800
You gonna be okay?

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:13.260
I'll contact you if I need help.

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:14.610
See ya.

00:23:03.940 --> 00:23:05.260
What sort of joke is this?

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.440
Everything's going smoothly so far.

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:07.370
We were supposed to meet up...

00:23:07.370 --> 00:23:08.240
Mushroom?

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:09.280
I think it's about time.

00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:09.930
A virus?

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:11.140
Stop? Why?

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:12.780
Which one is the real one?

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:15.080
Good luck with the next distraction.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
#08  Trick Play
